From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Oct 2026 14:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: sun55i-dsi-combo: use the captured analog values

The ANA0/ANA4 trim and the HS_CLK_CONT bit position were derived by decoding
the BSP dsi_dphy_open() field by field. A live register capture of the vendor
firmware, taken on the same board while its panel is lit and scanning, gives
different values for all three:

                  decoded      captured
  TX_CTL bit      26           28
  ANA0 (0x4c)     0x00000044   0x00000077
  ANA4 (0x5c)     0x844635ee   0x84363538

The hardware sides with the capture. With the decoded values the PHY status
register (0xe0) reads 0x07700000; with the captured ones it reads 0x15c55555,
which is exactly what the vendor firmware shows while driving the panel. So
the field decode is wrong somewhere, and the comment claiming otherwise is
removed.

This does not by itself put an image on the panel - that is still being
chased elsewhere in the pipeline - but it is independently verifiable: dump
0x5509000 before and after and compare 0xe0 against the capture in
docs/STOCK-DSI-REGISTERS.md.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5 [Claude Code]
Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun55i-dsi-combo.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun55i-dsi-combo.c
index d42d96e..9bc70cf 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun55i-dsi-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun55i-dsi-combo.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_GCTL_MODULE_EN		BIT(0)
 
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_TX_CTL		0x04
-#define SUN55I_DPHY_TX_CTL_HS_CLK_CONT		BIT(26)
+#define SUN55I_DPHY_TX_CTL_HS_CLK_CONT		BIT(28)
 
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_TX_TIME0		0x10
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_TX_TIME0_HS_TRAIL(n)	(((n) & 0xff) << 24)
@@ -115,14 +115,16 @@
  * these from the BSP phy_config[] *table*, whose ANA0/ANA4 layout does NOT match
  * this SoC (it even mislabelled ANA0 as lptx_setr/setc) -> wrong trim/LDO bias,
  * which together with the ENLDOR misdefine above left the DISPLL analog dead.
- *   ana0: reg_plr=4 [7:4], reg_sfb=1 [3:2]                          -> 0x44
- *   ana4: txpusd=2 txpusc=3 txdnsd=2 txdnsc=3 tmsd=1 tmsc=1 ckdv=3
- *         vtt_set=3 dmplvd=4 ib=2 en_mipi=1                         -> 0x844635ee
+ * The decode above gave ana0=0x44, ana4=0x844635ee and HS_CLK_CONT at bit 26.
+ * A live register capture of the vendor firmware taken while the panel is lit
+ * disagrees on all three, and the hardware sides with the capture: with these
+ * values the PHY status register (0xe0) reads 0x15c55555, exactly as stock,
+ * where the decoded values left it at 0x07700000.
  *   combo0: en_cp | en_comboldo | en_mipi                           -> 0x0b (correct)
  */
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_TX_TIME0	0x0406000e
-#define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_ANA0		0x00000044
-#define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_ANA4		0x844635ee
+#define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_ANA0		0x00000077
+#define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_ANA4		0x84363538
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_COMBO0		0x0000000b
 #define SUN55I_DPHY_CFG_COMBO1		0x00000043
 
-- 
2.47.3

